-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Atic Atac
  Publisher   Ultimate
  Version     1.4

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Atic Atac (1983)(Ultimate Play The Game)[a8][a8].z80
  MD5         06b11e63d60401666332a61626a5789c

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    The knight, wizard and serf, and most monsters, in fuller colour
              with more detail; the knight gets a red hat and green tunic. A
              few monsters turn a duller brown. Source: enhanced colours from
              an older Spec256 conversion (the MVV package), painter not
              established.

  Pace        original (+0.83% measured in JNext 1.2.0 and 1.1.104, 10 runs
              per scene)

  Changes     1.1: faster hooks (an image cache, row lookups), no picture
              change. 1.2: door and furniture cells no longer flash red next
              to moving figures; the menu's screen clear no longer leaves the
              icons on screen. 1.3: option QAOP + Space keys (Q A O P to move,
              Space to fire, Caps Shift pauses). 1.4: original pace, never
              faster (limiter).

  Note        Plays at the original's pace, never faster: a limiter makes each
              figure's drawing take the original's time, waiting on the video
              line for what the sprites save. With QAOP + Space on, Space
              fires, so only Caps Shift pauses. Known issues: quiet play
              measured +14.5% in JNext, set by which enemies turned up (runs
              without them -0.3 to +1.2%); enemies differ from run to run even
              on the same keys, because the game takes chance from the R
              register, which the hooks change; the game reads a few ROM bytes
              as data and gets the Next ROM's values, not the 48K ROM's (found
              by replay; effect on play not established); not yet checked in
              full on NextZXOS v2.10: it lacks the start-up fix for v2.10's
              ROM changes that Cyclone and Chuckie Egg needed. Missing: a
              quiet-play pace check with the same enemies in both games;
              hardware untested.

