-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      Played by the owner in JNext 2026-11-06: approved

  Replay      Original-game lockstep IDENTICAL on walk1, walk2 and t for all
              four v1.4 builds (default, Enhanced, each with QAOP + Space):
              21003 frames each, 40623 figure setups, 666275 rows, 45.1M
              sprite pixels; every hook ran (setups, rows, clears, room line,
              scenery drawers and op writers, text, character setup, figure
              painter, keys, pause). The limiter waits inside the replay (the
              video line modelled from the clock); R is not compared, as in
              v1.3 (the hooks change it). Units per colour set: 1483 cases, 3
              negative controls and 22 rework negatives detected, 432
              incoming-clock cases pass; limiter 72 cases (interrupts off and
              on, 0 and 20 lines ahead), limiter removed detected 36 of 36;
              toggle keys 924 / 832 cases pass, both toggle negatives
              detected; 3 replay negatives on t detected.

  Emulator    JNext 1.2.0 and 1.1.104 headless (v2.09 card, read-only): the
              four bare builds reach play and the player moves; the menu build
              reaches play. Flicker, 3 windows of 300 frames against the
              original: 0 out of step, 0 vanished, one-frame attribute changes
              0 / 1 (a room change) / 0 frames (original 77 / 26 / 70). Soak
              15 emulated minutes: no freeze, loop or crash; play in many
              rooms, game overs and restarts. No hardware test. No on-device
              NXC-loader test.

  Coverage    Same target, loading screen, default and Enhanced pattern bytes,
              trainers and credit as v1.0/v1.1. v1.1 hook-speed engine plus:
              the figure painter's nine LD (HL),E vacated-cell writes are NOPs
              (as its LD (HL),D writes already were), and the whole-screen
              clear 0x80B4 is hooked. Original game logic, sound and delays
              byte-exact; the only changed game-bank bytes are those ten
              sites. v1.4: the same game-bank bytes as v1.3; the hook code
              adds the pace limiter (figure setups, text, scenery, room line
              and character setup hooks) and hook RAM 0x5BA9-0x5BAF.

  Hardware    none

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
